	(text "Load cell inputs J12 / J13 + RC filters (CIF §8a)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "4ed7f32c-3c29-5fc5-8c36-01752e666485")
	)
	(text "J12 SIG (KF250NH 3-pin):\n1 SIG+ green, 2 SIG- white, 3 shield.\nJ13 EXC (KF250NH 3-pin):\n1 EXC+ red, 2 EXC- black, 3 shield.\nShields: yellow, GND here only.\nTension cells may swap SIG+ / SIG-:\nfix the sign in firmware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 68.58 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "7f68ce06-31f0-50f9-9166-30cd3d0c330d")
	)
	(text "D20 / D21 BAV199 (≤ 5 nA, typ. pA): clamp the ADC\ninputs to GND / AVDD after the 100 Ω, so an ESD hit\non the cable can't drive them past the rails (ADS1232\nis 750 V HBM). Leakage × ≈ 0.2 kΩ source ≪ 1 µV."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 116.84 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "9ffe9f0f-7924-5af5-a59a-47d5d2f28ac9")
	)
	(text "Signal and reference filters: 100 Ω per leg, 100 nF C0G across, 10 nF to GND (CIF §8a).\nThe reference gets the same network so both time constants match (TI SBAS350 §8.2).\nREFP / REFN are sensed at J13 pins 1 / 2: route them as their own pair from the\nconnector pads, not from the 5 V / GND planes. C26 = PGA bypass (pins 9-10)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 145.54 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "70330570-957a-52fc-9d2b-649c48fab5ce")
	)
	(text "U8 ADS1232 24-bit bridge ADC (TI SBAS350 weigh-scale configuration)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 22.86 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "872443b2-d0ae-5260-a5f6-f6faa3a95df3")
	)
	(text "A0 = GND (channel 1). GAIN1 / GAIN0 = 1 / 1 → gain 128, ±19.5 mV at a 5 V reference. SPEED = GND → 10 SPS, rejects 50 and 60 Hz.\nTEMP = GND. CLKIN = GND → internal oscillator, XTAL2 open. Unused channel 2 inputs to GND (TI weigh-scale example).\nAVDD = +5V via FB2 = bridge excitation → ratiometric. AVDD range 2.7-5.3 V (SBAS350 §5.3).\nPDWN (PA6) and SCLK (PA5) have 100k pull-downs: the ADC stays powered down until the firmware runs the power-up sequence.\nDRDY/DOUT → PA4. PA4 / PA5 are 3.6 V-max pins: fine, all ADC logic runs at 3.3 V. Input common mode 2.5 V (needs 1.5-3.5 V at gain 128)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 137.16 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "15d91840-4209-5f15-bf29-a3775c06ff68")
	)
	(text "Load cell firmware (CIF §8b, TI SBAS350 §7.4.5)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 172.72 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "e146187d-f2a0-5b79-b053-870952b487f0")
	)
	(text "Power-up: keep PA6 (PDWN) LOW until +5V and 3V3 are stable, wait ≥ 10 µs, then PDWN HIGH ≥ 26 µs, LOW ≥ 26 µs, HIGH.\nRead: wait for DRDY/DOUT LOW, clock 24 bits on SCLK (MSB first, two's complement). Clocking 26 bits instead also runs the\noffset self-calibration: do it after power-up and when the temperature changes. Discard the first conversions after power-up or reset.\n\nScale: 2 × SOP SOPLF-102 (1.5 t, 1.5 mV/V) summed in the junction box → 7.5 mV full scale at 5 V ≈ 38 % of ±19.5 mV, ≈ 2.5 µV per kg.\nBridge current ≈ 13 mA (two 780 Ω cells) from +5V. Warn at 1.5 t, alarm at 2.0 t total. Re-calibrate the scale factor (the old HX711\nfactor was taken at 3.3 V). Filtering as before: 0.5 kg noise threshold, ±0.25 kg stability window, 0.1 kg rounding.\n\n5 V load cell only: J13 pin 1 is the +5V rail through FB2. Never land a 24 V wire on J12 / J13\n(same push-in terminal type as the relay and sensor outputs): mark them \"5V LOAD CELL\" on the silk.\nExcitation comes from +5V (Power sheet: URB2405S → PTC → ferrite pi filter), the same rail as the module."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 177.8 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "ba5a7786-14ae-5891-9f7a-30ea147ec4f5")
	)
